-import type { Finding } from "../finding.page-type.ts"
-
-export const activitySetComposesAPageTheTrackingLandingRefuses = {
-  id: "01a072cb-d221-76bc-bc7d-1471081af607",
-  pageTypeSlug: "finding",
-  slug: "activity-set-composes-a-page-the-tracking-landing-refuses",
-  domainSlug: "domain/tracking",
-  claim:
-    "`activity-set` cannot land. `activity-default` composes a `session-activity` page under `alan/tracking/session-activities/pages/`, and the tracking landing refuses every path outside `alan/tracking/daily/wake-days/pages/` and `alan/tracking/food-entries/pages/`, so the compose always succeeds and the landing always throws. The command page states that boundary itself: its help says the tracked trees are the wake days and the food entries. Eighteen session-activity pages are on disk and `session-leveling` reads a difficulty off them, so the data is load-bearing and only the writer is barred. Widening the tracked trees changes what a command may reach, which is why this is written down rather than made.",
-  evidence:
-    "Read at HEAD 6a9d4f503a. `tracking-landing.module.code.ts:13-17` declares `DAYS_AT` as `alan/tracking/daily/wake-days/pages/`, `FOOD_ENTRIES_AT` as `alan/tracking/food-entries/pages/`, and `TRACKED_AT` as those two alone. `trackedIn` at :23 answers true only where a path starts with one of them, and `landingTracked` at :48 refuses before anything is written. `activity-default.module.code.ts:119-126` composes with `pageTypeSlug: session-activity` and hands `composed.put.path` to `landTracking`, turning its refusal into a throw at :91.\n\nThe conversion at 1ddec4e2b4 did not introduce this. That commit moved the guard out of the command into an importable module unchanged; before it the same two trees were spelled in the command's own code, and the caller reached them by spawning `akasha tracking`, which applied the same guard. The behaviour is preserved exactly and is now visible.\n\nWhat I did not establish: when it broke. `git log -S TRACKED_AT` reaches 28f9db7e0b on 2026-09-01, but the trees may have been spelled otherwise before that. The eighteen pages under `session-activities/pages/` are touched by one commit only, 648fe2d287 on 2026-09-03, whose message is `flatten structure` — a move rather than a creation. So they were written elsewhere by something else, and I did not find what.\n\nSeparately and not part of this defect: the help examples, the error text at :99 and the commit prefix `ops-tracking` at :15 all still name the deleted CLI.",
-} as const satisfies Finding
